remote.hint.log_in [hint]: Log git in:
remote.hint.or_ssh [hint]: Or add an ssh key to {ssh_dir} and switch to the ssh address: {ssh_dir}: string, the SSH key directory (fixed), ~/.ssh
remote.hint.log_in_or_ssh [hint]: Log git in to that host, or add an ssh key to {ssh_dir} and switch to the ssh address: {ssh_dir}: string, the SSH key directory (fixed), ~/.ssh
remote.hint.have_key [hint]: You have an ssh key, so the same repository can be reached over ssh:
remote.hint.to_switch [hint]: To switch:
remote.prompt.switch [prompt]: Switch to it? {choice} {choice}: string, the yes or no prompt keys (fixed), [Y/n]
remote.status.kept_https [status]: Kept {https}. To switch later: {https}: string, the HTTPS transport (fixed), https
remote.success.reachable [success]: reachable {url} {url}: string, the remote URL as git has it
remote.hint.first_save [hint]: Nothing committed yet. This commits and pushes:
remote.warning.waiting [warning]: The remote has new commits. Commit or discard the changes here, then:
remote.success.pushed [success]: pushed the repo is backed up
remote.status.up_to_date [status]: Already backed up: the remote has every commit.
inbox.header.clear [success]: nothing needs you. Home is in order.
inbox.header.count [inbox]: {n:# thing needs|# things need} you {n}: int, a count
inbox.more [hint]:   ...and {n} more: {n}: int, a count
inbox.done.heading [status]:   Done for you since you last looked:
inbox.next_hint [hint]:   Do the first one now:
inbox.nudge [nudge]: {bot}: {n:# thing needs|# things need} you{urgent}, run: {n}: int, a count; {urgent}: string, inbox.nudge.urgent or empty; {bot}: string, the persona's display name; homebot in the neutral voice
inbox.notify.title [notification]: {bot} needs you {bot}: string, the persona's display name; homebot in the neutral voice
inbox.notify.body [notification]: {title}{more}. Run: {title}: string, the first urgent item's title; {more}: string, inbox.notify.more or empty
inbox.notify.more [notification]:  (+{n} more) {n}: int, a count
inbox.unpack_preview [inbox]: It runs every step without asking; to see them first: {self}{preview} {self}: string, the command word: the name when one works on this machine, else homebot (filled by the renderer); {preview}: string, the preview command suffix (fixed),  unpack --dry-run
inbox.broken.title [inbox]: Could not check {check} {check}: string, internal check id printed verbatim: secrets, links, triage, git or profile
inbox.no_identity.title [inbox]: Git doesn't know who you are
inbox.no_identity.detail [inbox]: Commits by {self}{save} and the hourly autosave fail without a name and email. {self}: string, the command word: the name when one works on this machine, else homebot (filled by the renderer); {save}: string, the save subcommand (fixed),  save
inbox.no_signing_key.title [inbox]: Commits are signed with {key_path}, which this machine doesn't have {key_path}: path, the ssh signing key path, ~-shortened
inbox.no_signing_key.detail [inbox]: Every commit fails until it's here. Restore it ({self}{unlock}), or stop signing on this machine only: {self}: string, the command word: the name when one works on this machine, else homebot (filled by the renderer); {unlock}: string, the unlock subcommand (fixed),  unlock
inbox.gitconfig_shadow.title [inbox]: {gitconfig} overrides the git config from the repo {gitconfig}: string, the global git config path (fixed), ~/.gitconfig
inbox.gitconfig_shadow.detail [inbox]: Git reads it after {repo_config}, so its name, email or signing win. Move it aside; {self}{cleanup} then shows it, and anything this machine needs goes in {local_config}. {self}: string, the command word: the name when one works on this machine, else homebot (filled by the renderer); {repo_config}: string, the repo git config path (fixed), ~/.config/git/config; {cleanup}: string, the cleanup subcommand (fixed),  cleanup; {local_config}: string, the machine-local git config path (fixed), ~/.config/git/config.local
inbox.blocked.title [inbox]: A commit was refused
inbox.tidy_failed.title [inbox]: Automatic {step_name} failed {ago} {step_name}: string, internal tidy step printed verbatim: guard, seal, export, autosave, sync or link; {ago}: duration, a relative time from format.ago.* (e.g. 'just now', '4m ago', '3h ago', '2d ago')
inbox.no_repo.title [inbox]: {repo} is not a git repository {repo}: path, the home repo folder, shortened to ~/... (e.g. ~/.home)
inbox.no_gitleaks.title [inbox]: {tool} is missing, so every commit is refused {tool}: string, the missing scanner (fixed), gitleaks
inbox.no_guard.title [inbox]: The commit guard is not installed
inbox.no_keys.title [inbox]: Secrets are not set up yet
inbox.secret_conflict.title [inbox]: {n:# secret|# secrets} changed here and on another machine {n}: int, a count
inbox.secret_locked.title [inbox]: {n:# secret is|# secrets are} still locked {n}: int, a count
inbox.secret_upstream.title [inbox]: {n:# secret|# secrets} changed on another machine {n}: int, a count
inbox.secret_unsealed.title [inbox]: {n:# secret|# secrets} not sealed yet {n}: int, a count
inbox.link_invalid.title [inbox]: {n:# layout error|# layout errors} in the repo; those parts aren't linked {n}: int, a count
inbox.link_conflict.title [inbox]: {n:# file is|# files are} in the way of links {n}: int, a count
inbox.link_pending.title [inbox]: {n:# link|# links} to make or fix {n}: int, a count
inbox.backups.title [inbox]: {n:# backup|# backups} that {self}{link} moved aside: compare, then delete or keep {self}: string, the command word: the name when one works on this machine, else homebot (filled by the renderer); {n}: int, a count; {link}: string, the link subcommand (fixed),  link
inbox.triage.title [inbox]: {n:# new thing|# new things} to sort: track, ignore or snooze {n}: int, a count
inbox.no_remote.title [inbox]: Not backed up: the repo has no remote
inbox.never_pushed.title [inbox]: Not backed up yet: nothing pushed to the remote
inbox.unreachable.title [inbox]: Last reached the remote {ago} {ago}: duration, a relative time from format.ago.* (e.g. 'just now', '4m ago', '3h ago', '2d ago')
inbox.diverged.title [inbox]: This machine and the remote both have new commits
inbox.unpushed.title [inbox]: {n:# commit|# commits} not pushed {n}: int, a count
inbox.behind.title [inbox]: {n:# new commit|# new commits} on the remote {n}: int, a count
inbox.uncommitted.title [inbox]: {n:# uncommitted change|# uncommitted changes} {n}: int, a count
inbox.no_profile.title [inbox]: No profile chosen for {host} {host}: string, this machine's host name
inbox.no_profile.detail [inbox]: Set {default_key} or {hosts_key} in {config_file} {default_key}: string, the default profile config key (fixed), profiles.default; {hosts_key}: string, the per-host profile config key (fixed), profiles.hosts; {config_file}: string, the homebot config file (fixed), homebot.yml
inbox.missing_profile.title [inbox]: Profile {profile} does not exist yet {profile}: string, a profile name (a file in manifests/profiles/ without .yml)
inbox.missing_profile.detail [inbox]: Write the steps that set up this machine
inbox.never_unpacked.title [inbox]: Profile {profile} was never unpacked here{last} {profile}: string, a profile name (a file in manifests/profiles/ without .yml); {last}: string, inbox.never_unpacked.last when another profile was unpacked, else empty
inbox.never_unpacked.last [inbox]:  (last unpacked: {other}) {other}: string, the profile unpacked here before
inbox.profile_changed.title [inbox]: Profile {profile} changed since the last unpack {profile}: string, a profile name (a file in manifests/profiles/ without .yml)
inbox.export_failing.title [inbox]: Export {name} is failing {name}: string, export name
inbox.no_helper.title [inbox]: The background helper is not installed
inbox.no_helper.detail [inbox]: It seals, exports, links and reminds you every hour
inbox.helper_stale.title [inbox]: The background helper last ran {ago} {ago}: duration, a relative time from format.ago.* (e.g. 'just now', '4m ago', '3h ago', '2d ago')
export.status.none [status]: No exports configured for this OS in {config}. {config}: string, the config file (fixed), homebot.yml
export.reason.not_installed [status]: {tool} is not installed {tool}: string, the name of an external program
export.error.exit [error]: exited with {code}{stderr} {code}: int, a process exit code; {stderr}: string, ': ' plus the last 3 stderr lines joined with spaces, or empty
export.error.empty_folder [error]: produced an empty folder; kept the previous {out} {out}: path, the output path, repo-relative
export.error.empty_file [error]: produced an empty file; kept the previous {out} {out}: path, the output path, repo-relative
export.error.out_is_folder [error]: wrote a file, but {out} is a folder; kept the folder. Remove it yourself, or give the export another {out_key} {out}: path, the output path, repo-relative; {out_key}: string, the export's output key (fixed), out
export.error.out_is_file [error]: wrote a folder, but {out} is a file; kept the file. Remove it yourself, or give the export another {out_key} {out}: path, the output path, repo-relative; {out_key}: string, the export's output key (fixed), out
export.error.kept_aside [error]: {error}
The previous export is kept at {path}. {error}: string, what failed, as the system said it; {path}: path, where the previous export is now (absolute): old/<out's name> inside the export's work folder
export.warning.left_behind [warning]: The temporary folder {path} could not be removed. It is safe to delete. {path}: path, the temporary folder (absolute)
export.error.unknown [error]: No export named {names} for this OS. Exports here: {known}. {names}: string, the unknown names, comma-joined; {known}: string, the export names for this OS, comma-joined, or export.word.none
tidy.status.locked [status]: Another tidy is running.
tidy.status.nothing [status]: Nothing to tidy.
tidy.status.inbox_count [status]: {n:# thing|# things} in the inbox. {n}: int, a count
tidy.did.guard [status]: installed the commit guard
tidy.did.sealed [status]: sealed {n:# secret|# secrets} {n}: int, a count
tidy.did.exported [status]: refreshed {outs} {outs}: string, changed export output paths, comma-joined
tidy.did.committed [status]: committed {n:# file|# files} {n}: int, a count
tidy.did.pulled [status]: pulled {n:# commit|# commits} {n}: int, a count
tidy.did.pushed [status]: pushed {n:# commit|# commits} {n}: int, a count
tidy.did.linked [status]: fixed {n:# link|# links} {n}: int, a count
setup.status.removed [status]: Background helper removed.
setup.success.guard [success]: installed commit guard ({hook_key}) {hook_key}: string, the git hook path key (fixed), core.hooksPath
setup.status.guard_present [status]: Commit guard already installed.
setup.warning.no_repo [warning]: {root} is not a git repo yet; skipped the commit guard. {root}: path, the home repo folder, shortened to ~/...
setup.success.helper [success]: installed {helper} {helper}: string, helper.description.systemd or helper.description.launchd
setup.hint.zshrc [hint]: Add this to your {zshrc} so new terminals tell you when something needs you: {zshrc}: string, the zsh startup file (fixed), .zshrc
helper.error.no_systemd [error]: No systemd user session here, so the hourly helper can't be installed.
Run this yourself, or from cron:
helper.error.systemctl [error]: {command}{args} failed. {args}: string, the systemctl arguments; {command}: string, the failed systemctl invocation prefix (fixed), systemctl --user
helper.error.launchctl [error]: {command} failed. {command}: string, the failed launchctl invocation (fixed), launchctl bootstrap
config.error.unknown_key [error]: {where}: unknown key "{key_name}" (expected {keys}) {where}: string, where in the file, e.g. 'homebot.yml: exports[0]' or 'manifests/profiles/x.yml step 3'; {key_name}: string, the unknown key; {keys}: string, allowed keys, comma-joined
